WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.021
- Now, do you have your dog
with you on tour all the time?

00:00:02.021 --> 00:00:04.343
- Madeline Kahn Chenoweth
has a bad heart now

00:00:04.343 --> 00:00:06.131
and she can't fly,

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.584
and I wish so badly I
could travel with her.

00:00:08.584 --> 00:00:10.070
I miss her when I'm not there,

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:13.112
but I do have a girl called
Natalie that stays with her--

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.808
- You almost called your
dog sitter Madeline.

00:00:14.808 --> 00:00:15.644
(laughs)

00:00:15.644 --> 00:00:17.785
Do you ever accidentally
call her Madeline,

00:00:17.785 --> 00:00:19.550
which is your dog's name?
- Probably.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:20.323
(laughs)
- Okay, that's alright.

00:00:20.323 --> 00:00:22.482
- Matalie, Matalie. Her name's Natalie.

00:00:22.482 --> 00:00:23.476
- Okay.

00:00:23.476 --> 00:00:27.405
(up-tempo music)

00:00:27.405 --> 00:00:29.471
- My two dogs, Larry and Pompom,

00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:31.034
Larry is what I call "special needs".

00:00:31.034 --> 00:00:32.754
- Don't say that about Larry.
- [Kathy] Sorry.

00:00:32.754 --> 00:00:34.046
- He can hear you.

00:00:34.046 --> 00:00:35.569
- I know, yes, okay.

00:00:35.569 --> 00:00:37.171
He's not the sharpest pencil in the box,

00:00:37.171 --> 00:00:38.843
but he's all love.
- [Kristin] He's the sweetest.

00:00:38.843 --> 00:00:40.190
His legs are getting weaker,

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:41.559
and so I just call him Wheels,

00:00:41.559 --> 00:00:42.790
'cause I think it's only a matter of time

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.949
before I just chop off his
legs and put those wheels on.

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:46.412
You know, the wheels on the
bus go 'round and 'round.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:48.339
But the bad thing is, my
house has a lot of stairs.

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:49.431
So the day that I--

00:00:49.431 --> 00:00:51.056
- I can't even go up and down them.

00:00:51.056 --> 00:00:53.332
- Exactly. So I think he'll
have wheels for like a day

00:00:53.332 --> 00:00:54.980
and then he'll just roll to his death.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.257
- Don't you have an elevator?

00:00:56.257 --> 00:00:57.673
- I do have an elevator,

00:00:57.673 --> 00:00:59.464
and you know what, I've
actually thought about--

00:00:59.464 --> 00:01:00.946
that's very Hollywood of me.

00:01:00.946 --> 00:01:03.806
I may use my elevator
for my dog with wheels.

